tly what startup does; the probe-request prerequisite and the result share the subject identity, and the same function is the only producer of that event. Oracle and environment dependence: the source-side defect is environment-independent - the dial error is discarded and the connection is dereferenced, which makes a nil dereference whenever the dial fails - while the observation demonstrates it in an environment of the class the claim names (no route to the probe address); the review therefore treats the observation as an instance of the stated applicability rather than as a claim about every deployment. Contrary evidence and limits: whether the project's own deployments reach the probe address is unknown and recorded in the claim; the check observes the helper rather than a completed replica construction, which additionally needs peer addresses and a listener; and the latency table's parsing and delay arithmetic are explicitly out of scope. No counterevidence was found that the helper returns an address in this scope.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the observation depends on the environment's ability to dial the probe address; the source defect is not environment-dependent but the witness is\\\",\n   \\\"the check exercises the helper, not a full replica construction, which also needs peer addresses and a listener\\\",\n   \\\"whether the project's deployments reach the probe address is unread\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-c11.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(sub['artifact_id'])\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-c11.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress